\section*{Aim}
To plot and analyze the transfer (Id–Vgs) and output (Id–Vds) characteristics of an NMOS transistor using Cadence Virtuoso with 90nm GPDK technology.

\section*{Objective}
\begin{itemize}
    \item To design an NMOS testbench in Virtuoso using the 90nm GPDK library.
    \item To obtain the transfer characteristics (Id vs. Vgs) at different values of Vds.
    \item To obtain the output characteristics (Id vs. Vds) at different values of Vgs.
    \item To extract NMOS parameters such as threshold voltage (Vth), transconductance (gm), output resistance (r\textsubscript{o}), channel-length modulation ($\lambda$), and Early voltage (V\textsubscript{A}).
\end{itemize}

\section*{Equipment / Software Used}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Cadence Virtuoso Schematic Editor
    \item ADE L / ADE XL Simulation Environment
    \item GPDK 90nm Technology Library
    \item ViVA Waveform Viewer
\end{itemize}
\\

\section*{Theory}

The NMOS transistor operates based on the voltage applied between its terminals. Two fundamental characteristics are studied:

\subsection*{1. Transfer Characteristics (Id--Vgs)}
The transfer characteristic relates the drain current $I_D$ to the gate voltage $V_{GS}$ for a fixed value of $V_{DS}$.

In saturation:
\[
I_D = \frac{1}{2}\mu C_{ox}\frac{W}{L}(V_{GS} - V_{th})^2 (1 + \lambda V_{DS})
\]

\subsection*{2. Output Characteristics (Id--Vds)}
The output characteristic relates the drain current $I_D$ to the drain voltage $V_{DS}$ for different values of $V_{GS}$.

Output resistance:
\[
r_o = \left( \frac{\partial I_D}{\partial V_{DS}} \right)^{-1}
\]

Channel-length modulation:
\[
\lambda = \frac{1}{V_A}
\]

Transconductance:
\[
g_m = \frac{\partial I_D}{\partial V_{GS}}
\]

\section*{Procedure (Simulation Steps)}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Create a new schematic in Virtuoso.
    \item Place an NMOS device from the gpdk090 library and set dimensions:
    \[
    W = 1\mu m,\quad L = 90nm
    \]
    \item Connect gate and drain to DC voltage sources (Vg and Vd), and connect source and bulk to ground.
    \item Open ADE L $\rightarrow$ Select DC Analysis.
    \item For transfer characteristics: Sweep $V_{GS}$ from 0 to 1.2\,V for fixed $V_{DS}$ values (e.g., 50\,mV and 1.2\,V).
    \item For output characteristics: Sweep $V_{DS}$ from 0 to 1.2\,V for different $V_{GS}$ values.
    \item Plot drain current $I_D$ using ViVA and extract parameters (Vth, gm, r\textsubscript{o}, $\lambda$).
\end{enumerate}
